780	+//! The `POST /v1/responses` proxy handler (SMA-769 D3–D5, D8, D13, D15, § 7.2).
781	+//!
782	+//! The route is mounted only when `[responses] enabled = true` (D8); otherwise it is a 404. The
783	+//! flow is the generic [`pipeline::proxy`]; this module gives the [`RESPONSES`] descriptor:
784	+//!
785	+//! - **Parse** (§ 7.2): a COPY of the body is read into [`ResponsesRequest`]. `input` must be a
786	+//!   string or an array. D4 (`background: true`) is refused always; D3 (a non-null
787	+//!   `previous_response_id`, `conversation` or `prompt`, or an `item_reference` input item) is
788	+//!   refused only when interception is on. The pipeline calls the parse before `Limits::admit`,
789	+//!   so a refused request uses no quota and is not charged. A JSON `null` and `background: false`
790	+//!   pass (Review Focus 2).
791	+//! - **D5:** the request body goes upstream byte-identical. The gateway does not set `store`.
792	+//! - **Usage** (D14): the Responses readers of [`responses_usage`](super::responses_usage).
793	+//! - **Terminal frame** (D13): [`RESPONSES_TERMINAL_SSE_ERROR`].
794	+//! - **Limits** (D15): the interception limits with the record and hold caps of `[responses]`.
795	+//!
796	+//! Streaming obeys the same `stream_enabled` switch as chat (D9): the pipeline reads the one
